# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Yuzhi Liu et al. (2026). Mixture of experts architectures for machine learning interatomic potentials.
#   npj Artificial Intelligence. doi:10.1038/s44387-026-00144-9
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 153a936fffe4ecb1...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 646 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liu2026mixture.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the mixture-of-experts DPA3 models introduced in the
# paper (registry method DPA3-MoE, origin) and the dense DPA3 baselines on
# OMol25, OC20M and OMat24, and the halved-dimension CHGNet baseline and
# its MoE-E extension on MPtrj with their stated test MAEs (Sec.
# 'Transferability to CHGNET'). DPA3 results are reported as normalised
# MAE ratios or only in figures, so they have no results.

