###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - DPA3 ablations report validation MAEs normalised by the 6-layer dense DPA3 (Table 1, Fig. 2; e.g. MoE-E with 64 experts 0.771 energy and 0.779 force); ratios are not encoded. Absolute OC20M/OMol25/OMat24 MAEs and RMSEs are only in Fig. 3 and Supplementary Note 2 (not read).
# - The 12-layer and 6x-parameter DPA3 baselines and global-routing variants are not encoded as runs; the CHGNet MoE-E with K = 2 and 4 is only in Supplementary Table 7.
# - The CHGNet MoE-E extension is kept under CHGNet; DPA3-MoE covers only the DPA3-based models.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liu2026mixture.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

